===Numeral===
{{head|en|numeral}}

# The [[cardinal number]] occurring after [[ten]] and before [[twelve]]. Represented as [[11]] in Arabic digits.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1973|author=Jane Roberts|title=The education of Oversoul Seven|page=8|passage=It was a thunderstormy morning, '''eleven''' o'clock, with great dashes of rain pounding against the windows.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Helen Bailey|title=Knowing Me, Knowing You
|passage=I know most girls say that they've known their bezzies since they started primary school together, bonding over handmade Mother's Day cards or a hatred of the egg-and-spoon race, but I've only known Taryn since I was '''eleven'''{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=w:Terry Pratchett|page=169
|title=A Slip of the Keyboard
|passage=It was also a work of fiction in which another work of fiction (''Gulliver's Travels'') was real; that Chinese box of an idea is wonderful to discover when you're '''eleven'''.}}

